sentences.l:
And they, as reapers face to face with one another
drive a swath along the plough-land of a blessed man,
of wheat or barley;

and the rim did not hold the spear for him, heavy with bronze,
but through it went, and through bone, and the brain
within, all of it, was spattered;

But he went, Isus and Antiphus to despoil,
the two sons of Priam, one a bastard and one true-born, both,
in one chariot being;

And as a lion of a swift hind the infant children
easily crushed, having seized them in strong teeth,
having come to the lair, and from them the tender heart took away;
